<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hargeisa</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hargeisa is the capital and largest city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-somaliland">Somaliland</a>, the self-declared republic in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somalia">Somalia</a>. It grew as a trading town and became the capital of British Somaliland in 1941. During the civil war, government forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siad-barre">Siad Barre</a> bombed it in 1988, killing thousands of Isaaq and destroying much of the city, which was rebuilt after Somaliland declared independence in 1991.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hargeisa.jpg" alt="Hargeisa" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Somaliland.com · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:HargeisaDrone.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
